<PageLayout title="About" kicker="Tech Talk with TimX" description="Tech Talk with TimX tells the stories behind what's being built, through long-form journalism and podcast conversations with founders and builders.">
  <p>Every product has a story behind it: the late nights, the pivots, the near-misses and the small wins nobody saw. Tech Talk with TimX exists to tell those stories properly.</p>
  <p>We publish long-form stories and podcast conversations with founders, engineers, designers and operators, from people writing their first line of code to teams scaling across continents. We care less about funding announcements and more about the decisions, doubts and lessons that shaped the work.</p>
  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Founder Files:</strong> how founders started, what nearly broke them and what they're building now.</li>
    <li><strong>Builder Diaries:</strong> the engineers, designers and product people behind the product.</li>
    <li><strong>The Pivot:</strong> the moment the plan changed, and what happened next.</li>
    <li><strong>Deep Dives:</strong> long reads on companies, markets and ideas.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who's behind it</h2>
  <p>Tech Talk with TimX is hosted by TimX. Every story is edited to the standards set out in our <a href="/editorial-standards">editorial standards</a>.</p>
  <h2>Get involved</h2>
  <p>If you're building something, <a href="/share-your-story">tell us your story</a>. If you'd like to reach our audience, see <a href="/advertise">advertising and partnerships</a>. For anything else, <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
